What:		/sys/bus/cxl/devices/hmu_memX.Y/hmu_memX.Y.Z/interrupts
Date:		October, 2026
KernelVersion:	v7.3
Contact:	linux-cxl@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		(RO) What the instance advertises. supported_modes,
		supported_access_types and interrupts are space separated names
		("overflow" and "level" for the two interrupt capabilities);
		supported_unit_sizes is in bytes and supported_downsampling in
		factors, both space separated; epoch_range_ms is "min max" in
		milliseconds; hotlist_size is in entries; capacity_ranges is the
		device capacity in 256 MiB units, the valid extent of the range
		bitmap; epoch_type is "global" or "per_counter"; address_overlap
		is 1 if this instance may count a range that overlaps a sibling
		instance's (a start whose range overlaps an active sibling's
		fails with -EBUSY unless both instances have it); epoch_range_ms
		shows 0 for a bound shorter than a millisecond;
		postponed_overflow is 1 if hot units survive a hotlist overflow.


What:		/sys/bus/cxl/devices/hmu_memX.Y/hmu_memX.Y.Z/counter_width
What:		/sys/bus/cxl/devices/hmu_memX.Y/hmu_memX.Y.Z/active
What:		/sys/bus/cxl/devices/hmu_memX.Y/hmu_memX.Y.Z/overflows
Date:		October, 2026
KernelVersion:	v7.3
Contact:	linux-cxl@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		(RO) State. counter_width is the width in bits of the access
		counter for the current unit_size, the bound of
		hotness_threshold; active is 1 while the instance is enabled;
		overflows counts the hotlist overflows the device reported since
		the last start.

